{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1422","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1422","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1422\",\"parent_revision\":\"eb41c20d1ec950044652b9c932b13500e610e4c1cd3f127f543da7c845f4556a\",\"root_revision\":\"eb41c20d1ec950044652b9c932b13500e610e4c1cd3f127f543da7c845f4556a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\noperations.py still directly imports `github_sync.SECTION_HEADING` and `github_sync._render_groomed` \u2014 these rendering utilities are not abstracted into the BacklogBackend protocol. Backends that don't use GitHub formatting (sqlite, memory) cannot customize section rendering. The protocol should include a `render_groomed_section(item) -> str` method and a `section_heading` property, or the rendering should be moved to a backend-neutral location.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-04-04T17:27:45Z \u2014 Replace snapshot with final RT-ICA after swarm completion</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Abstract rendering utilities from github_sync into BacklogBackend protocol\\nDate: 2026-04-04\\nGoal: Remove operations.py coupling to github_sync rendering symbols by moving them into the BacklogBackend protocol.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. operations.py currently imports github_sync.SECTION_HEADING and/or github_sync._render_groomed | Status: DERIVABLE (initial grep returned no matches \u2014 coupling may not exist as described or may use different symbols)\\n2. BacklogBackend protocol (backend_protocol.py) currently lacks render_groomed_section and section_heading | Status: DERIVABLE\\n3. The three backends (github, sqlite, memory) exist | Status: AVAILABLE (confirmed by file listing)\\n4. Type checker (ty) is configured in pyproject.toml | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Existing tests cover github_sync rendering path | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Any other callers of github_sync rendering symbols outside operations.py | Status: DERIVABLE\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 4\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T17:27:45Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Abstract rendering utilities from github_sync into BacklogBackend protocol\\nDate: 2026-04-04\\nGoal: Remove operations.py coupling to github_sync rendering symbols by moving them into the BacklogBackend protocol.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. operations.py directly imports github_sync rendering symbols | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read \u2014 line 30 imports SECTION_HEADING and _render_groomed with aliases; confirmed by fact-checker\\n2. BacklogBackend protocol lacks render_groomed_section and section_heading | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read backend_protocol.py \u2014 methods absent; confirmed by fact-checker\\n3. Three backends (github, sqlite, memory) exist | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Glob confirmed\\n4. ty type checker configured in pyproject.toml | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Project config\\n5. Existing tests cover github_sync rendering path | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst found 5 tests in tests/test_github_sync.py targeting _render_groomed\\n6. All callers of github_sync rendering symbols identified | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst mapped 16 systems in Impact Radius\\n7. (new) Design choice for sqlite/memory default rendering | Status: DERIVABLE | Citation: options are clear (plain-text passthrough, shared utility, or minimal markdown subset); implementer decision\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 1: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (fact-checker read line 30 directly)\\n- Condition 2: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (fact-checker verified protocol)\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (impact-analyst found test file)\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (impact-analyst mapped 16 systems)\\n- Condition 7: (new) DERIVABLE \u2014 design decision for non-GitHub backend rendering defaults\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE-with-clear-options. No MISSING conditions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCODE_CHANGE (required):\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py \u2014 add 2 abstract methods to BacklogBackend Protocol (HIGH)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py \u2014 remove github_sync rendering imports at line 30; replace usage at lines 2295-2296 and 2420 with protocol dispatch (HIGH)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py \u2014 implement render_groomed_section and section_heading delegating to existing github_sync functions (MEDIUM)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py \u2014 implement both methods with backend-neutral defaults (MEDIUM, design decision required)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py \u2014 implement both methods with backend-neutral defaults (MEDIUM, design decision required)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py \u2014 keep existing symbols; add backward-compat note (LOW)\\n\\nTEST_UPDATE:\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py \u2014 migrate 5 tests off _render_groomed to GitHubBackend protocol interface (HIGH)\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py \u2014 add rendering coverage test (LOW)\\n\\nVERIFY_COMPATIBLE (no changes expected):\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/_branch_delegates.py\\n\\nCONTENT_UPDATE (documentation):\\n- plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md \u2014 fix false claim line 80; document new protocol methods (MEDIUM)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md \u2014 update import pattern description (MEDIUM)\\n- plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md \u2014 add one-line note that rendering is now part of protocol contract (LOW)\\n- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md \u2014 strike FIND-22 entry (LOW)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nIf not done:\\n- operations.py continues to violate the BacklogBackend abstraction boundary by importing directly from github_sync\\n- SQLite and InMemory backends permanently cannot customize section rendering\\n- docs/backend-providers.md line 80 remains a false claim (states operations.py never imports from github_sync \u2014 it does)\\n- Any future backend implementation will inherit broken rendering dispatch by default\\n- test_github_sync.py tests remain coupled to the wrong abstraction level\\n\\nWhen done:\\n- operations.py depends only on the BacklogBackend protocol \u2014 no github-specific imports\\n- All backends control their own rendering; SQLite/InMemory get backend-neutral defaults they can override\\n- docs/backend-providers.md false claim becomes true\\n- FIND-22 in DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md resolves automatically\\n- The protocol contract is complete; future backends implement render_groomed_section and section_heading at construction time\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py::SECTION_HEADING` - dict defined at line 43, exported in `__all__` (line 24); currently the sole definition of section heading labels. After the refactor these labels move to the protocol or a backend-neutral location. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Current definition site \u2014 moving the symbol breaks the import in `operations.py:30` and any future direct callers; backward-compat alias or re-export needed during transition.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py::_render_groomed` - function defined at line 134; renders `GroomedData` as markdown. Currently the sole implementation of this behavior. Used both internally (line 204) and by `operations.py` (line 2420). | Risk: HIGH | Why: Moving or wrapping this function is the core action of this item; all callers must migrate to the new protocol method.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` - imports `SECTION_HEADING as _SECTION_HEADING_MAP` and `_render_groomed as _render_groomed_md` from `github_sync` at line 30; uses `_SECTION_HEADING_MAP` at lines 2295\u20132296 and `_render_groomed_md` at line 2420. This is the direct coupling the item targets. | Risk: HIGH | Why: The import must be removed and replaced with a call through the BacklogBackend protocol \u2014 operations.py must receive the backend and call `backend.render_groomed_section()` and `backend.section_heading` instead.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py` - imports the `github_sync` module at line 12 and delegates to it. Must implement the new `render_groomed_section` and `section_heading` protocol methods by wrapping the existing `github_sync` functions. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: This backend already owns the GitHub rendering path; adding protocol method implementations that delegate to the existing `github_sync` functions is low-risk but mandatory.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` - imports `backend_protocol.get_config` (line 32) and uses `operations` module (line 29). Does not use rendering symbols directly but calls operations functions that do. | Risk: LOW | Why: No direct rendering coupling; will benefit automatically once operations.py is fixed, but no changes needed in server.py.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py::BacklogBackend` - Protocol class at line 143; currently lacks `render_groomed_section` and `section_heading`. Adding these as abstract protocol methods is the structural change this item requires. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Adding new abstract methods to a Protocol is a breaking contract change \u2014 all three concrete backend implementations (GitHub, SQLite, InMemory) must implement the new methods or `ty` will report protocol violations.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py::SQLiteBackend` - implements `BacklogBackend` at line 118. Will need to implement `render_groomed_section` and `section_heading`. SQLite has no GitHub formatting context. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Needs a stub, default, or backend-neutral implementation; if the protocol change ships without this, `ty` check fails.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py::InMemoryBackend` - implements `BacklogBackend` at line 78. Same situation as SQLiteBackend. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Needs stub or default rendering implementation; test double must satisfy the protocol or tests using InMemoryBackend will fail type checking.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/_branch_delegates.py` - imports `get_config` from `backend_protocol` (line 7). Does not use rendering symbols. | Risk: LOW | Why: No rendering coupling; not affected by new protocol methods.\\n\\n### Tests\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py` - directly tests `_render_groomed` via `test_render_groomed_heading` (line 91), `test_render_groomed_subsection_as_h3` (line 98), `test_render_groomed_subsection_content` (line 106), `test_render_groomed_canonical_order` (line 113), and `test_render_empty_sections_no_section_headings` (line 439). Imports from `backlog_core.github_sync` directly. | Risk: HIGH | Why: If `_render_groomed` moves or is wrapped, these tests target the wrong abstraction level \u2014 they must be updated to test the backend protocol interface or moved to test the GitHubBackend implementation.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py` - imports `_resolve_groomed_content` and `groom_item` from `backlog_core.operations` (line 23). Exercises the groom path which calls `_render_groomed_md` internally. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: No direct rendering assertion but exercises the code path; if the rendering dispatch is broken during refactor, these integration-level tests will surface it.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` - exercises operations broadly; no direct rendering symbol references found. | Risk: LOW | Why: Indirect coverage \u2014 rendering is exercised through groom_item; test updates unlikely unless operation signatures change.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py` - tests backend interop; no direct rendering references found. | Risk: LOW | Why: May need a new test to verify that all backends produce consistent rendering through the new protocol, but existing tests do not assert rendering behavior.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` - line 80 explicitly states that `operations.py` \\\"never import[s] from `gh_client`, `github_sync`, or `github_branches` directly\\\" \u2014 this claim is currently FALSE (operations.py:30 imports two symbols from github_sync). After this item ships, the claim becomes TRUE. Line 100 documents the BacklogBackend Protocol but does not mention rendering methods. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Needs updating to (a) remove the now-false caveat once operations.py is fixed, and (b) document the new `render_groomed_section` and `section_heading` protocol methods.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` - documents module import patterns and responsibilities (lines 42\u201343 on operations.py and backlog.py). The comment in `backend_protocol.py` (line 13) documents what imports it. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Architecture documentation describes `operations.py` as not importing from `github_sync` \u2014 currently inaccurate. Must be updated to reflect the new protocol-based rendering dispatch once the fix ships.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` - line 414 briefly documents the BacklogBackend Protocol and its backends. | Risk: LOW | Why: Minimal mention; may need one-line note that rendering is now part of the protocol contract.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md` - drift audit document noting import inconsistencies in operations.py (FIND-22, line 449). After fix, the `github_sync` coupling in operations.py disappears, resolving one drift finding. | Risk: LOW | Why: Audit document; will auto-become-accurate after the fix \u2014 no required update, but maintainers should strike FIND-22 if it references this coupling.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- None identified. CI runs the full test suite; test failures from broken rendering dispatch will surface automatically. No CI workflow files reference rendering symbols directly.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n- None identified. No agent or skill files were found to reference `SECTION_HEADING`, `_render_groomed`, or the rendering path.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py` | Role: producer | Connection: defines both symbols being abstracted (`SECTION_HEADING`, `_render_groomed`) | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: imports and uses both rendering symbols; direct coupling being removed | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` | Role: producer | Connection: BacklogBackend Protocol must gain `render_groomed_section` and `section_heading` abstract methods | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: implements BacklogBackend; must add the two new protocol methods | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: implements BacklogBackend; must implement new rendering protocol methods | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: implements BacklogBackend; must implement new rendering protocol methods | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py` | Role: test | Connection: directly tests `_render_groomed` via 5 test methods; imports from `backlog_core.github_sync` | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py` | Role: test | Connection: exercises groom_item which calls rendering path | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` | Role: test | Connection: exercises operations broadly; no direct rendering assertions | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py` | Role: test | Connection: backend interop tests; no rendering assertions \u2014 gap in coverage | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: claims operations.py never imports from github_sync (currently false); documents BacklogBackend Protocol | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: documents module import patterns; must reflect operations.py no longer importing from github_sync | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: brief mention of BacklogBackend Protocol | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: FIND-22 records operations.py import coupling being fixed | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/_branch_delegates.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: imports get_config from backend_protocol; no rendering coupling | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: imports backend_protocol and uses operations module indirectly | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` - adding abstract protocol methods is a breaking contract change requiring all three backend implementations to be updated atomically\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` - the direct import coupling being removed; must be replaced with protocol dispatch without breaking the groom and section-heading paths\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_github_sync.py` - 5 tests target `_render_groomed` directly; they will break or become redundant when the symbol moves\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - compatibility (protocol contract change breaks all three backend implementations simultaneously)\\n  - verification (tests test the wrong abstraction level; no cross-backend rendering coverage)\\n  - documentation (backend-providers.md contains a currently-false claim that becomes true after this fix)\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - The three backend implementations (github, sqlite, memory) were implied by the item description but their specific update burden was not quantified. SQLite and InMemory have no native rendering concept \u2014 they will need backend-neutral defaults (e.g., plain-text or pass-through), making this a design decision, not just a code move.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (SQLite/InMemory rendering default needed)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBlocked by (must complete first):\\n- P389 (backlog-pluggable-backend) \u2014 COMPLETE (commit a2b56597). This item is a direct follow-on from P389; no further prerequisite work required.\\n- Design decision \u2014 SQLite/InMemory backend-neutral rendering default must be decided before implementation begins. Options: plain-text passthrough, shared utility function, or minimal markdown subset. Decision owner should be captured before dispatch.\\n\\nVerify before closing:\\n- If github_sync._render_groomed is removed rather than kept: audit external callers not found in Impact Radius scan (aliased imports may have masked additional usages).\\n\\nThis item may unblock:\\n- #473 MCP prompts \u2014 unverified. If MCP prompts expose section rendering to tool callers, they depend on consistent rendering across backends. Verify whether #473 has a rendering dependency before closing this item.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nP1 \u2014 confirmed. 16 systems in scope, 5 rated HIGH risk, breaking protocol contract change requiring atomic update of all 3 backend implementations. A false claim in docs/backend-providers.md is actively misleading implementers. Not deferrable without accruing further confusion as the protocol grows.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] operations.py line 30 imports zero symbols from github_sync for rendering (grep confirms)\\n- [ ] backend_protocol.py defines render_groomed_section(self, item: GroomedData) -> str and section_heading as abstract protocol methods\\n- [ ] GitHubBackend, SQLiteBackend, and InMemoryBackend each implement both new methods; ty reports zero protocol violations\\n- [ ] All 5 tests previously targeting github_sync._render_groomed directly (test_render_groomed_heading, test_render_groomed_subsection_as_h3, test_render_groomed_subsection_content, test_render_groomed_canonical_order, test_render_empty_sections_no_section_headings) pass after migration to GitHubBackend protocol interface\\n- [ ] test_groom_mark_groomed.py and test_backlog_core_operations.py pass without modification\\n- [ ] test_cross_backend.py has at least one new test asserting all 3 backends return a non-empty string from render_groomed_section\\n- [ ] docs/backend-providers.md line 80 claim is accurate (operations.py no longer imports from github_sync) and new protocol methods are documented\\n- [ ] backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md updated to reflect operations.py no longer importing from github_sync\\n- [ ] uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/ exits 0\\n- [ ] uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/ exits 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMedium. The mechanical scope is well-defined (6 code files, 2 test files, 4 doc files) but three factors add non-trivial complexity:\\n\\n1. Atomic protocol change \u2014 Adding abstract methods to BacklogBackend must ship with all 3 backend implementations in the same commit. Partial application fails ty and breaks CI. No incremental path.\\n\\n2. Design decision: SQLite/InMemory rendering defaults \u2014 SQLite and InMemory have no GitHub context. The implementer must choose between: (a) plain-text fallback, (b) delegating to github_sync._render_groomed directly (defeats the abstraction), or (c) a shared _default_render_groomed utility in a backend-neutral module. This decision must be