eature-verifier on QG-T2)\\n- [ ] INFO: ty reports 69 pre-existing frozen-property diagnostics \u2014 zero related to #1422 changes (reported by feature-verifier on QG-T2)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-04-04T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRefactor only. No CLI changes, no new user-visible behavior, no data migration, no schema changes.\\n\\nIn scope:\\n- Add render_groomed_section(item) -> str and section_heading abstract methods to BacklogBackend protocol\\n- Remove rendering imports from operations.py; replace with protocol dispatch\\n- Implement both methods in all 3 backends (github wraps existing functions; sqlite/memory provide backend-neutral defaults \u2014 design decision required before implementation)\\n- Migrate 5 tests in test_github_sync.py from testing _render_groomed directly to testing GitHubBackend protocol interface\\n- Add cross-backend rendering test to test_cross_backend.py\\n- Update 4 documentation files\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- Removing _render_groomed from github_sync.py (keep for backward compat)\\n- Changing rendering output format\\n- MCP server changes\\n- Any work in server.py, _branch_delegates.py (verified compatible, no changes needed)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] LOW: AC criterion 6 specifies test_cross_backend.py but cross-backend render_groomed_section test lives in backlog_core/tests/test_rendering.py \u2014 VERIFIED: behavioral coverage is present and passing. File location diverges from AC literal text but is not a defect. (reported by feature-verifier on QG-T2, processed 2026-05-21)\\n- [x] INFO: Pre-existing test failure test_spawn.py::test_build_spawn_shell_cmd_returns_interactive_argv_without_p_flag \u2014 unrelated to #1422, pre-existing. (reported by feature-verifier on QG-T2, processed 2026-05-21)\\n- [x] INFO: ty reports 69 pre-existing frozen-property diagnostics \u2014 zero related to #1422 changes. (reported by feature-verifier on QG-T2, processed 2026-05-21)\\n\\n## Evidence Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll four claims are **VERIFIED** \u2014 the coupling described in the issue DOES exist in the current code.\\n\\n### Claim 1: operations.py directly imports github_sync.SECTION_HEADING\\n**VERIFIED**\\n- File: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py`\\n- Line 30: `from .github_sync import SECTION_HEADING as _SECTION_HEADING_MAP, _render_groomed as _render_groomed_md`\\n- Evidence: Direct import of `SECTION_HEADING` constant (aliased as `_SECTION_HEADING_MAP`)\\n\\n### Claim 2: operations.py directly imports github_sync._render_groomed  \\n**VERIFIED**\\n- File: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py`\\n- Line 30: `from .github_sync import SECTION_HEADING as _SECTION_HEADING_MAP, _render_groomed as _render_groomed_md`\\n- Evidence: Direct import of private function `_render_groomed` (aliased as `_render_groomed_md`)\\n\\n### Claim 3: BacklogBackend protocol lacks render_groomed_section method and section_heading property\\n**VERIFIED**\\n- File: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py`\\n- Grep search for `render_groomed_section|section_heading`: No matches found\\n- Evidence: Protocol defines 65+ methods but neither method mentioned in claims exists\\n\\n### Claim 4: sqlite and memory backends cannot customize section rendering\\n**VERIFIED (by implication)**\\n- Both backends declare: `class SQLiteBackend` and `class InMemoryBackend` implement `BacklogBackend` Protocol\\n- Since the Protocol has no `render_groomed_section` method (Claim 3), neither backend can customize it\\n- Evidence: The Protocol is the contract \u2014 if a method is absent from the Protocol, implementations cannot add it without breaking contractual guarantees\\n</div>\\n\\n## Critical Finding\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**The grep for `github_sync\\\\.(SECTION_HEADING|_render_groomed)` initially returned no matches because the imports use aliased names.** The aliasing masked the coupling at first search. Direct inspection of line 30 revealed the actual imports.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe coupling is **real and present**. The issue accurately describes a tightly-coupled rendering system where `operations.py` depends directly on github_sync rendering constants and functions, while the BacklogBackend protocol lacks the abstraction needed for alternative backends to customize this behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:54339926198b96a7d235caa421144184 -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"37f34b466ac7a84d138a4ffcad1493c99624bf7f8b8fabaa32e824266740111f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCRbPg\"}"}